{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/979330-approximating-the-lunar-charmset-with-rearranged-solar-charms","id":979330,"title":"Approximating the Lunar Charmset with rearranged Solar Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-30T16:50:51-07:00","id":979330,"title":"Approximating the Lunar Charmset with rearranged Solar Charms","content":"How many people actually try this when they homebrew Lunars, or quickly mock them up for a game?<br /> <br /> For example, trying to model a branch of Lunar Strength Charms with something similar to Triple-Distance Throwing Technique, followed by Charms which are similar to Iron Raptor Technique, Strength-Hying Heave, and Crashing Wave Throw?<br /> <br /> (The logic of that progression being that it's easier to start with throwing thing that are designed to be thrown, and then working your way into throwing things which are not.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:00:42-07:00","id":979411,"title":"","content":"I'd potency-check them against Solar Charms, but not approximate them with Solar Charms. That's like combining the worst mistakes of 1e and 2e Lunar Charm design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:40:44-07:00","id":979459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/979330-approximating-the-lunar-charmset-with-rearranged-solar-charms?p=979411#post979411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd potency-check them against Solar Charms, but not approximate them with Solar Charms. That's like combining the worst mistakes of 1e and 2e Lunar Charm design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean that you wouldn't ALTER them to fit.<br /> <br /> That's why I said &quot;something LIKE Triple-Throwing Distance Technique&quot; and the like.<br /> <br /> When I tried to write a Strength-based version of Iron Raptor Technique, the first thing I threw out was the &quot;return to sender&quot; effect, and then I made it hit harder. Because the Charm would be about hurling a non-projectile weapon with superhuman strength without any particular technique to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's more like using the Solar Charmset as a guide to say, &quot;Okay, THESE all seem like Strength-based effects, THIS is the rough order I'd put them in, and NOW I'm going to change the individual effects to fit the aesthetic&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:53:07-07:00","id":979462,"title":"","content":"Well, at least with what I'm doing, I do use the Solar charms as...kind of a reference? Not as a baseline or anything like, but as the areas I sort of need to cover and what maps to what Attribute. There's also the though I have that some Lunar charms should just be more flexible in their application.<br /> <br /> The idea, at least for me, is to limit things as little as possible unless I have to for a specific effect. There are Strength based thrown charms yes, but you can use thrown plenty fine with Perception and Dex effects as well. (I am aiming for each Attribute getting a combat tree, and two Utility trees.<br /> <br /> At least that's my perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/336-monkoflords","name":"MonkofLords","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:41:21-07:00","id":979490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/979330-approximating-the-lunar-charmset-with-rearranged-solar-charms?p=979459#post979459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean that you wouldn't ALTER them to fit.<br /> <br /> That's why I said &quot;something LIKE Triple-Throwing Distance Technique&quot; and the like.<br /> <br /> When I tried to write a Strength-based version of Iron Raptor Technique, the first thing I threw out was the &quot;return to sender&quot; effect, and then I made it hit harder. Because the Charm would be about hurling a non-projectile weapon with superhuman strength without any particular technique to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's more like using the Solar Charmset as a guide to say, &quot;Okay, THESE all seem like Strength-based effects, THIS is the rough order I'd put them in, and NOW I'm going to change the individual effects to fit the aesthetic&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of one way to achieve the weapon returning effect that's appropriately Lunar. It involves a spring-loaded tongue, a la chameleons and Orochimaru. It probably wouldn't be related to a distance-increasing Charm for ranged weapons, though (among other things that said hypothetical Charm might do.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:52:33-07:00","id":979498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/979330-approximating-the-lunar-charmset-with-rearranged-solar-charms?p=979490#post979490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can think of one way to achieve the weapon returning effect that's appropriately Lunar. It involves a spring-loaded tongue, a la chameleons and Orochimaru. It probably wouldn't be related to a distance-increasing Charm for ranged weapons, though (among other things that said hypothetical Charm might do.).</div> </div> </div> </div>What about that spider-Lunar in the comic who used her own silk to tether and retrieve her weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:01:44-07:00","id":979502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/979330-approximating-the-lunar-charmset-with-rearranged-solar-charms?p=979498#post979498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about that spider-Lunar in the comic who used her own silk to tether and retrieve her weapons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd view the spinnerets as the Charm, and attaching a thread to it to be a more involved sub-process of using the Charm. It would lack distance, and possibly take some time to get moving at sufficient speed in order to attack, as the thread lacks muscle and flesh to make it move like a limb, to say nothing of the apparatus used by lizards formerly labeled as Iguania to launch their tongues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T22:48:16-07:00","id":979519,"title":"","content":"I wrote an Essence 4 midboss-type encounter as Mastered Dreaming Pearl and White Reaper, with a dash of dirty tricks. She didn't actually know the martial arts, they just provided approximate imitations of a Changing Moon's flirty tease / guiltless destroyer of cities aspects. The players seemed to enjoy the encounter!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:00:15-07:00","id":979631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkofLords</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/979330-approximating-the-lunar-charmset-with-rearranged-solar-charms?p=979462#post979462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are Strength based thrown charms yes, but you can use thrown plenty fine with Perception and Dex effects as well. (I am aiming for each Attribute getting a combat tree, and two Utility trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for Perception, I'm thinking that Lunars could bring back First Edition's &quot;Blood-Singing Instincts&quot; as a more flexible version of the Solar Archery Charm, &quot;Blood Without Balance&quot;.<br /> <br /> BWB lets a Solar archer make a reflexive Aim action and act earlier than their Initiative if she becomes the beneficiary of a Distract gambit. &quot;Blood-Singing Instincts&quot; would let a Lunar do the same with any sort of attack, like a wolf taking advantage of a packmate's feint.<br /> <br /> Solar Charms are efficient -- Archery Charms do what is best for archery, which means providing for Aim actions, which Melee and Brawl don't bother dealing with. Holden said that Lunar Charms were going to come off as &quot;less polished&quot; than Solar Charms, and he might have even said &quot;less efficient&quot;. It's still a Charm that can be used with archery and throwing attacks, and Aim bonuses are still useful for close range attacks, but it's not as focused as BWB and its not directly linked to Charms that extend range, provide ammunition or even bows, or turn arrows into explosives.<br /> <br /> <br /> But Lunars CAN pack all of their perceptive Charms under just one Trait. Awareness, Investigation, Socialize, Occult, Medicine, and more.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T08:13:43-07:00","id":979668,"title":"","content":"So would the Lunar equivalent of Elements-Sculpted Avatar still have its bonus against Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T07:26:35-07:00","id":980233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/979330-approximating-the-lunar-charmset-with-rearranged-solar-charms?p=979668#post979668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would the Lunar equivalent of Elements-Sculpted Avatar still have its bonus against Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>My thoughts regarding that Solar are better expressed in another thread.<br /> <br /> But I am excited about how Lunars could use Perception Charms to learn exactly what forms best please or terrify their targets, and use Heart's Blood and Appearance Charms to take those forms.<br /> <br /> That sounds more effective and interesting than an extra dot of Appearance... Though Shaping the Ideal Form or a following Charm might do that too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:30:17-07:00","id":983664,"title":"","content":"If a Lunar ever throws down against the PCs in my game, I'll use the QC provided and toss Solar charms on top of it.<br /> <br /> Mostly, my NPCs operate in narrative space. They don't have to track mote expenditure for every little thing. For that, I make a 2nd Edition Lunar and describe what the charms/knacks are doing.<br /> <br /> I don't need to create the mechanics for a charm that allows the Lunar to eat anything they can fit in their mouth or lactate poppy milk. I just tell the players that's what the Lunar is doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T06:19:26-07:00","id":983881,"title":"","content":"Must admit i have been kind of lazy when it comes to NPC exalts - for starters because i tend to play the Chosen as something of a quite rare breed. With their numbers at the tens of thousands at most - and the Terrestrials filling the lion's share of this total - through the whole of Creation, spirits, god-bloods, mortal sorcerers and thaumaturgists tend to make for far more numerous antagonists or associates touching on the supernatural, meaning i spend far more time toying with mixing &amp; matching or tinkering spirit charms.<br /> <br /> When i do feel the need for some extra color/weirdness in the powers of a NPC, be it a elemental, demon, fae, ghost, god, sorcerer or exalt, i either rake others of their kind (recombining stuff between the full moon warrior and the changing moon trickster for example) or throw in a bunch of stuff taken from Sorcery, martial arts charms and merits according to taste.<br /> <br /> Also, evocations - the fact some shaping rituals or control spells can give a NPC, be it exalt, mortal or spirit, acess to a whole new set of custom powers opens room for a not insignificant venue for homebrewed insanity. In fact i ended up developing a sort of &quot;exigent/terrestrial wannabe&quot; antagonists through them in the Bezoari, a race of people with a natural affinity for hearthstones and gathering power from them that works in ways akin to the gifts and mysteries of the Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}